msgstr "Try a shorter word, or clear the filter."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "An organizer creates an election on a public contract, the registry."
msgstr "An organizer creates an election on a public contract, the registry."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Voters send encrypted ballots. They are added up while still encrypted, and only the final total is decrypted."
msgstr "Voters send encrypted ballots. They are added up while still encrypted, and only the final total is decrypted."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Nodes called sequencers group the votes into batches and record each batch on the chain with a proof that it was counted correctly."
msgstr "Nodes called sequencers group the votes into batches and record each batch on the chain with a proof that it was counted correctly."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "What each batch changed is published, so anyone can check what was counted without trusting the sequencers."
msgstr "What each batch changed is published, so anyone can check what was counted without trusting the sequencers."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Who does what"
msgstr "Who does what"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "DAVINCI is a voting protocol in which every step of the count is proven. Four parties take part in an election, which the registry and this explorer call a <0>process</0>:"
msgstr "DAVINCI is a voting protocol in which every step of the count is proven. Four parties take part in an election, which the registry and this explorer call a <0>process</0>:"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "<0>The organizer</0> creates the election on the <1>registry</1> contract, <2>ProcessRegistry</2>, and sets its rules."
msgstr "<0>The organizer</0> creates the election on the <1>registry</1> contract, <2>ProcessRegistry</2>, and sets its rules."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "<0>Voters</0> encrypt their ballots in their voting app and send them to a sequencer."
msgstr "<0>Voters</0> encrypt their ballots in their voting app and send them to a sequencer."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "<0>Sequencers</0> collect the votes, prove them in batches and record each batch on the registry (in technical terms, they settle it)."
msgstr "<0>Sequencers</0> collect the votes, prove them in batches and record each batch on the registry (in technical terms, they settle it)."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "<0>The key holder</0> decrypts the final total when voting ends, and that step is proven too. It is one sequencer, or a <1>key committee</1> of independent operators (davinci-dkg)."
msgstr "<0>The key holder</0> decrypts the final total when voting ends, and that step is proven too. It is one sequencer, or a <1>key committee</1> of independent operators (davinci-dkg)."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "This explorer reads what was recorded from the chain: the registry’s events, the transactions that recorded each batch and the data blobs they carry, which a beacon node serves. What only a sequencer can tell (whether a vote is still pending, receipts for votes, data the beacon has already deleted) is labelled as coming from a sequencer."
msgstr "This explorer reads what was recorded from the chain: the registry’s events, the transactions that recorded each batch and the data blobs they carry, which a beacon node serves. What only a sequencer can tell (whether a vote is still pending, receipts for votes, data the beacon has already deleted) is labelled as coming from a sequencer."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "An election is created"
msgstr "An election is created"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The organizer creates the election on the registry and fixes its rules: when voting opens and closes, how many people may vote at most, what a valid ballot looks like (the <0>ballot rules</0>), who may vote (the <1>list of voters</1>) and who holds the key that will decrypt the results (the <2>key mode</2>). The registry gives the election a unique <3>process id</3>."
msgstr "The organizer creates the election on the registry and fixes its rules: when voting opens and closes, how many people may vote at most, what a valid ballot looks like (the <0>ballot rules</0>), who may vote (the <1>list of voters</1>) and who holds the key that will decrypt the results (the <2>key mode</2>). The registry gives the election a unique <3>process id</3>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The registry then takes a <0>fingerprint</0> of the starting state itself. Every later state grows from it, so none of these rules can be swapped afterwards."
msgstr "The registry then takes a <0>fingerprint</0> of the starting state itself. Every later state grows from it, so none of these rules can be swapped afterwards."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The title, the question and the names of the options are not on the chain. They are in a description document the organizer publishes, and the registry records its address and its fingerprint (the <0>metadata hash</0>). The explorer shows the document’s text as the organizer’s only when the two match. The organizer can publish a new version until voting ends; a version published while voting was open is flagged, because votes cast before it were cast under the previous one."
msgstr "The title, the question and the names of the options are not on the chain. They are in a description document the organizer publishes, and the registry records its address and its fingerprint (the <0>metadata hash</0>). The explorer shows the document’s text as the organizer’s only when the two match. The organizer can publish a new version until voting ends; a version published while voting was open is flagged, because votes cast before it were cast under the previous one."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The organizer calls <0>newProcess</0> with the voting window, the maximum number of voters, the ballot mode, the census and the key mode. The process id is the organizer’s address, a 4-byte prefix of this registry and a 7-byte per-organizer nonce."
msgstr "The organizer calls <0>newProcess</0> with the voting window, the maximum number of voters, the ballot mode, the census and the key mode. The process id is the organizer’s address, a 4-byte prefix of this registry and a 7-byte per-organizer nonce."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The fingerprint is the <0>genesis state root</0>: the root of a SHA-256 sparse Merkle tree with six leaves (the process id, the packed ballot mode, a hash of the encryption key, an empty results accumulator, the census origin and the ballot VK hash)."
msgstr "The fingerprint is the <0>genesis state root</0>: the root of a SHA-256 sparse Merkle tree with six leaves (the process id, the packed ballot mode, a hash of the encryption key, an empty results accumulator, the census origin and the ballot VK hash)."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The chain knows a ballot only as numbers in fields. <0>newProcess</0> records the metadata document’s address together with its metadata hash, the SHA-256 of its exact bytes, and the explorer downloads the document and hashes it. New versions go through <1>setProcessMetadata</1> until voting ends; after that the document is frozen. Every version stays on the registry’s log."
msgstr "The chain knows a ballot only as numbers in fields. <0>newProcess</0> records the metadata document’s address together with its metadata hash, the SHA-256 of its exact bytes, and the explorer downloads the document and hashes it. New versions go through <1>setProcessMetadata</1> until voting ends; after that the document is frozen. Every version stays on the registry’s log."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Every election on this registry, with its rules"
msgstr "Every election on this registry, with its rules"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Voters send encrypted ballots"
msgstr "Voters send encrypted ballots"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The voting app encrypts each answer before it leaves the device, so the <0>ballot</0> travels and is stored as numbers only the key holder could read. With it, the app sends a <1>ballot proof</1>: a proof that the encrypted ballot follows the rules of the election, which does not reveal what it says."
msgstr "The voting app encrypts each answer before it leaves the device, so the <0>ballot</0> travels and is stored as numbers only the key holder could read. With it, the app sends a <1>ballot proof</1>: a proof that the encrypted ballot follows the rules of the election, which does not reveal what it says."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The app signs the ballot, adds the voter’s proof of being on the list of voters and sends everything to a sequencer. It shows the voter a <0>vote id</0>, the number to find the vote again later."
msgstr "The app signs the ballot, adds the voter’s proof of being on the list of voters and sends everything to a sequencer. It shows the voter a <0>vote id</0>, the number to find the vote again later."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "A ballot is 16 ElGamal ciphertexts on the BabyJubJub curve, encrypted under the process key; the ballot mode says how many of them carry values and which values are allowed. The ballot proof is a Groth16 proof of the davinci-circom circuit that the ballot is a correct encryption for this process. Its inputs hash commits to the process id, the ballot mode, the key, the voter’s address, the vote id, the ciphertexts and the voter’s weight."
msgstr "A ballot is 16 ElGamal ciphertexts on the BabyJubJub curve, encrypted under the process key; the ballot mode says how many of them carry values and which values are allowed. The ballot proof is a Groth16 proof of the davinci-circom circuit that the ballot is a correct encryption for this process. Its inputs hash commits to the process id, the ballot mode, the key, the voter’s address, the vote id, the ciphertexts and the voter’s weight."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The client signs the vote id with the voter’s Ethereum key and sends ballot, proof, signature and census proof to a sequencer."
msgstr "The client signs the vote id with the voter’s Ethereum key and sends ballot, proof, signature and census proof to a sequencer."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Sequencers batch them"
msgstr "Sequencers batch them"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "A <0>sequencer</0> checks each ballot as it arrives, so that one bad ballot cannot spoil a whole <1>batch</1>. It closes a batch when enough votes are waiting or the oldest has waited long enough: at most 1024 votes, and at most one per voter."
msgstr "A <0>sequencer</0> checks each ballot as it arrives, so that one bad ballot cannot spoil a whole <1>batch</1>. It closes a batch when enough votes are waiting or the oldest has waited long enough: at most 1024 votes, and at most one per voter."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Before storing the ballots it scrambles their encryption with a fresh secret (<0>re-encryption</0>), so nobody can match a stored ballot to the one a voter sent. It also refreshes some stored ballots that did not change, so that a changed vote does not stand out. <1>Changing your vote, privately</1> explains both."
msgstr "Before storing the ballots it scrambles their encryption with a fresh secret (<0>re-encryption</0>), so nobody can match a stored ballot to the one a voter sent. It also refreshes some stored ballots that did not change, so that a changed vote does not stand out. <1>Changing your vote, privately</1> explains both."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The sequencer checks every ballot the way the zkVM guest will: ballot proof, signature, census proof and inputs hash. A batch holds at most one vote per ballot slot."
msgstr "The sequencer checks every ballot the way the zkVM guest will: ballot proof, signature, census proof and inputs hash. A batch holds at most one vote per ballot slot."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "For each batch it draws a fresh secret seed, re-encrypts every ballot from it, silently re-randomizes other occupied slots, and builds the state-tree updates, the data blobs and the public values it expects the proof to produce."
msgstr "For each batch it draws a fresh secret seed, re-encrypts every ballot from it, silently re-randomizes other occupied slots, and builds the state-tree updates, the data blobs and the public values it expects the proof to produce."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Sequencers and the accounts that recorded batches"
msgstr "Sequencers and the accounts that recorded batches"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "One proof per batch"
msgstr "One proof per batch"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "One program checks the whole batch, and its run is proven: the result is a small <0>proof</0> that the chain can check quickly instead of redoing the work. The program checks every ballot proof, every signature and every voter’s place on the list of voters, stores the ballots and updates the encrypted total."
msgstr "One program checks the whole batch, and its run is proven: the result is a small <0>proof</0> that the chain can check quickly instead of redoing the work. The program checks every ballot proof, every signature and every voter’s place on the list of voters, stores the ballots and updates the encrypted total."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "What the proof makes public (its <0>public values</0>) is a short summary: the fingerprints of the state before and after, how many votes and changed votes the batch holds, and whether every check passed."
msgstr "What the proof makes public (its <0>public values</0>) is a short summary: the fingerprints of the state before and after, how many votes and changed votes the batch holds, and whether every check passed."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The program is the vote-batch <0>guest</0>, running in the ZisK <1>zkVM</1>. In one execution it checks every ballot proof, every signature, census membership, the state-tree updates, every re-encryption and silent refresh, the homomorphic tally and the layout of the data blobs."
msgstr "The program is the vote-batch <0>guest</0>, running in the ZisK <1>zkVM</1>. In one execution it checks every ballot proof, every signature, census membership, the state-tree updates, every re-encryption and silent refresh, the homomorphic tally and the layout of the data blobs."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The ZisK proof is wrapped into a <0>PLONK proof</0>: 768 bytes of proof plus 512 bytes of public values, whatever the size of the batch. The public values are the guest’s output registers: the state roots before and after, the census root, the vote and overwrite counts, the blob digest and count, <1>occupied_before</1>, and the <2>ok</2> flag with its <3>fail_mask</3>."
msgstr "The ZisK proof is wrapped into a <0>PLONK proof</0>: 768 bytes of proof plus 512 bytes of public values, whatever the size of the batch. The public values are the guest’s output registers: the state roots before and after, the census root, the vote and overwrite counts, the blob digest and count, <1>occupied_before</1>, and the <2>ok</2> flag with its <3>fail_mask</3>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Every value with its meaning."
msgstr "Every value with its meaning."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The decoded public values of a recent batch"
msgstr "The decoded public values of a recent batch"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The batch is recorded, with its data"
msgstr "The batch is recorded, with its data"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The sequencer sends the batch and its proof to the registry in one transaction. The registry records it only if the proof is valid, the batch starts from the latest state of the election, its voters were checked against the right list of voters and the voter limit holds. The election then moves to its new state. In technical terms the batch is settled, and a recorded batch is a <0>state transition</0>."
msgstr "The sequencer sends the batch and its proof to the registry in one transaction. The registry records it only if the proof is valid, the batch starts from the latest state of the election, its voters were checked against the right list of voters and the voter limit holds. The election then moves to its new state. In technical terms the batch is settled, and a recorded batch is a <0>state transition</0>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The same transaction carries the batch’s data in <0>data blobs</0>: the new vote ids, every ballot the batch wrote (still encrypted) and the new encrypted total. It shows when a voter’s ballot place is used for the first time and, with a list of voters built from addresses, whose place it is. It does not show whether a voter who had already voted changed their vote or only had their stored ballot refreshed."
msgstr "The same transaction carries the batch’s data in <0>data blobs</0>: the new vote ids, every ballot the batch wrote (still encrypted) and the new encrypted total. It shows when a voter’s ballot place is used for the first time and, with a list of voters built from addresses, whose place it is. It does not show whether a voter who had already voted changed their vote or only had their stored ballot refreshed."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The sequencer sends <0>submitStateTransition</0> as an EIP-4844 blob transaction. The registry verifies the PLONK proof against its pinned <1>program vk</1>, checks that the batch starts at the process’s latest root, that the census root and the occupied-slot count match, that the voter limit holds, and that each blob opens to the value the guest computed. Then the process’s <2>latestStateRoot</2> moves to the new root and the registry emits <3>ProcessStateTransitioned</3>."
msgstr "The sequencer sends <0>submitStateTransition</0> as an EIP-4844 blob transaction. The registry verifies the PLONK proof against its pinned <1>program vk</1>, checks that the batch starts at the process’s latest root, that the census root and the occupied-slot count match, that the voter limit holds, and that each blob opens to the value the guest computed. Then the process’s <2>latestStateRoot</2> moves to the new root and the registry emits <3>ProcessStateTransitioned</3>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "A slot’s first write is public because refreshes only touch occupied slots; with a Merkle census the slot follows from the voter’s address, so who voted and when is public. What stays hidden is which occupied slots were overwritten and which were only refreshed."
msgstr "A slot’s first write is public because refreshes only touch occupied slots; with a Merkle census the slot follows from the voter’s address, so who voted and when is public. What stays hidden is which occupied slots were overwritten and which were only refreshed."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Every check before a batch is recorded, in order"
msgstr "Every check before a batch is recorded, in order"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Anyone can rebuild the state"
msgstr "Anyone can rebuild the state"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Anyone may record batches (settlement is permissionless), so several sequencers can serve one election. A sequencer that loses a race, and an <0>observer</0> that never records batches, rebuild each batch from its published data and accept it only if replaying it gives the new fingerprint the registry recorded. Anyone can do the same, without asking a sequencer, to check that what was counted is what was recorded."
msgstr "Anyone may record batches (settlement is permissionless), so several sequencers can serve one election. A sequencer that loses a race, and an <0>observer</0> that never records batches, rebuild each batch from its published data and accept it only if replaying it gives the new fingerprint the registry recorded. Anyone can do the same, without asking a sequencer, to check that what was counted is what was recorded."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "When voting ends, the <0>encrypted total</0> is decrypted and published as the results. The protocol decrypts only that final total, never a single ballot. The key holder could still decrypt any ballot or any earlier total from the published data, which is why the key mode matters."
msgstr "When voting ends, the <0>encrypted total</0> is decrypted and published as the results. The protocol decrypts only that final total, never a single ballot. The key holder could still decrypt any ballot or any earlier total from the published data, which is why the key mode matters."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "With a sequencer key, the sequencer that holds the key decrypts the total and proves the decryption with a second program. The registry checks that proof, and that it was made on the election’s final state."
msgstr "With a sequencer key, the sequencer that holds the key decrypts the total and proves the decryption with a second program. The registry checks that proof, and that it was made on the election’s final state."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "With a committee key, the key committee decrypts the total together, after the registry has checked it against the final state. Each of their steps carries a proof."
msgstr "With a committee key, the key committee decrypts the total together, after the registry has checked it against the final state. Each of their steps carries a proof."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The accumulator is state leaf <0>0x04</0>. With a sequencer key the second program is the results guest, and the registry verifies its proof against <1>resultsProgramVK</1> and checks it was made on the process’s final root. With a DKG key a davinci-dkg committee threshold-decrypts it after the registry has checked the accumulator against the final root; every partial decryption and every combine carries a Groth16 proof."
msgstr "The accumulator is state leaf <0>0x04</0>. With a sequencer key the second program is the results guest, and the registry verifies its proof against <1>resultsProgramVK</1> and checks it was made on the process’s final root. With a DKG key a davinci-dkg committee threshold-decrypts it after the registry has checked the accumulator against the final root; every partial decryption and every combine carries a Groth16 proof."

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "The results of a finished election"
msgstr "The results of a finished election"

#: src/pages/learn/content/HowItWorks.tsx
msgid "Read on: <0>how results are produced</0> and <1>who holds the key</1>."
msgstr "Read on: <0>how results are produced</0> and <1>who holds the key</1>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Ballots are encrypted to one key per election. Whoever holds the matching secret could read the ballots, and is the one who can publish the results. There are three choices: one sequencer holds it, a key committee holds it in shares, or the committee and the organizer each hold a part."
msgstr "Ballots are encrypted to one key per election. Whoever holds the matching secret could read the ballots, and is the one who can publish the results. There are three choices: one sequencer holds it, a key committee holds it in shares, or the committee and the organizer each hold a part."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Why the key matters"
msgstr "Why the key matters"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Every ballot is encrypted to the <0>election key</0>. Whoever can use the matching secret could open any ballot in the published data, and is the one who can publish the results. The organizer decides who that is when creating the election (the <1>key mode</1>). The programs that check the batches are the same in every mode."
msgstr "Every ballot is encrypted to the <0>election key</0>. Whoever can use the matching secret could open any ballot in the published data, and is the one who can publish the results. The organizer decides who that is when creating the election (the <1>key mode</1>). The programs that check the batches are the same in every mode."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Mode"
msgstr "Mode"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Who holds the secret"
msgstr "Who holds the secret"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "How the results come out"
msgstr "How the results come out"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
#: src/protocol/types.ts
msgid "Sequencer key"
msgstr "Sequencer key"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "One sequencer node, the one that handed out the key."
msgstr "One sequencer node, the one that handed out the key."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "That node decrypts the total and proves the decryption is correct."
msgstr "That node decrypts the total and proves the decryption is correct."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
#: src/protocol/types.ts
msgid "Committee, automatic"
msgstr "Committee, automatic"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Nobody holds it whole: each member of a key committee holds one share."
msgstr "Nobody holds it whole: each member of a key committee holds one share."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Enough committee members decrypt together, once voting has ended."
msgstr "Enough committee members decrypt together, once voting has ended."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
#: src/protocol/types.ts
msgid "Committee, organizer-locked"
msgstr "Committee, organizer-locked"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The committee, plus a secret the organizer keeps."
msgstr "The committee, plus a secret the organizer keeps."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The committee decrypts only after the organizer reveals its secret."
msgstr "The committee decrypts only after the organizer reveals its secret."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The key mode is chosen in <0>newProcess</0>. The organizer only ever talks to the registry; in the DKG modes the davinci-dkg committee sits behind it. The zkVM guests are the same in every mode; with a sequencer key the node proves the tally with the results guest."
msgstr "The key mode is chosen in <0>newProcess</0>. The organizer only ever talks to the registry; in the DKG modes the davinci-dkg committee sits behind it. The zkVM guests are the same in every mode; with a sequencer key the node proves the tally with the results guest."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The organizer asks a sequencer for the key before creating the election. That sequencer is then the only one that can publish the results, and it could also open every ballot in the published data. This mode trusts one node with ballot secrecy: it suits testing, and organizers who accept that trust."
msgstr "The organizer asks a sequencer for the key before creating the election. That sequencer is then the only one that can publish the results, and it could also open every ballot in the published data. This mode trusts one node with ballot secrecy: it suits testing, and organizers who accept that trust."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The request is <0>POST /processes/keys</0>, for the process id the organizer is about to create. The node derives the secret from its own master secret and the process id, so it stores nothing per process, and a key handed out for one id is useless under any other. The results come out through a results proof."
msgstr "The request is <0>POST /processes/keys</0>, for the process id the organizer is about to create. The node derives the secret from its own master secret and the process id, so it stores nothing per process, and a key handed out for one id is useless under any other. The results come out through a results proof."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The key comes from a <0>key committee</0> of independent operators, which creates keys together so that no member ever knows a whole secret: each holds one share. No sequencer and no organizer holds the secret."
msgstr "The key comes from a <0>key committee</0> of independent operators, which creates keys together so that no member ever knows a whole secret: each holds one share. No sequencer and no organizer holds the secret."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "After voting ends, anyone can ask for the results; sequencers ask on their own shortly after the end. The registry first checks that the encrypted total is the one in the election’s final state, then hands it to the committee. Enough members (the <0>threshold</0>) decrypt it together, each step with a proof."
msgstr "After voting ends, anyone can ask for the results; sequencers ask on their own shortly after the end. The registry first checks that the encrypted total is the one in the election’s final state, then hands it to the committee. Enough members (the <0>threshold</0>) decrypt it together, each step with a proof."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The process key is one of the <0>pool keys</0> of a davinci-dkg <1>epoch</1>. The registry’s adapter registers a DKG application for the process on the newest Live epoch with a free pool key, and the key of the process is that pool key."
msgstr "The process key is one of the <0>pool keys</0> of a davinci-dkg <1>epoch</1>. The registry’s adapter registers a DKG application for the process on the newest Live epoch with a free pool key, and the key of the process is that pool key."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Sequencers ask for the decryption on their first heartbeat after the end. The registry checks the encrypted tally against the final state root and hands one ciphertext per ballot field to the committee; each member’s partial decryption carries a Groth16 proof."
msgstr "Sequencers ask for the decryption on their first heartbeat after the end. The registry checks the encrypted tally against the final state root and hands one ciphertext per ballot field to the committee; each member’s partial decryption carries a Groth16 proof."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The key combines a committee key with a key of the organizer’s. The organizer receives its secret (the <0>organizer secret</0>) when creating the election, and the registry never stores it. The committee cannot start decrypting until the organizer reveals the secret, so the organizer decides when the results appear, but not what they are."
msgstr "The key combines a committee key with a key of the organizer’s. The organizer receives its secret (the <0>organizer secret</0>) when creating the election, and the registry never stores it. The committee cannot start decrypting until the organizer reveals the secret, so the organizer decides when the results appear, but not what they are."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Losing the organizer secret loses the results."
msgstr "Losing the organizer secret loses the results."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The secret can be revealed at any time. An organizer that reveals it while voting is open leaves the election with the trust of the automatic mode."
msgstr "The secret can be revealed at any time. An organizer that reveals it while voting is open leaves the election with the trust of the automatic mode."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The organizer’s proof of owning its key names the committee round, so the organizer picks the round when creating the election."
msgstr "The organizer’s proof of owning its key names the committee round, so the organizer picks the round when creating the election."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The process key is the pool key plus the organizer key, <0/>. The organizer’s secret <1/> is returned to the organizer at creation and never stored by the registry. The committee’s partial decryptions do not begin until the organizer calls <2>revealProcessKey</2> with it. The organizer’s proof of possession binds the epoch, so a locked process names its epoch; apps read it from the adapter’s <3>registrationEpoch()</3>."
msgstr "The process key is the pool key plus the organizer key, <0/>. The organizer’s secret <1/> is returned to the organizer at creation and never stored by the registry. The committee’s partial decryptions do not begin until the organizer calls <2>revealProcessKey</2> with it. The organizer’s proof of possession binds the epoch, so a locked process names its epoch; apps read it from the adapter’s <3>registrationEpoch()</3>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "What the key committee never does"
msgstr "What the key committee never does"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The committee never rebuilds the election’s secret, which would open every ballot in the published data. It decrypts only the final total, one encrypted number per ballot field. A field whose encrypted total is still empty (as in an election that never counted a ballot) decrypts to 0 under any key, so the registry records 0 for it without asking the committee."
msgstr "The committee never rebuilds the election’s secret, which would open every ballot in the published data. It decrypts only the final total, one encrypted number per ballot field. A field whose encrypted total is still empty (as in an election that never counted a ballot) decrypts to 0 under any key, so the registry records 0 for it without asking the committee."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The committee threshold-decrypts only the final accumulator, one ciphertext per ballot field. An empty field is one whose ciphertext is the identity."
msgstr "The committee threshold-decrypts only the final accumulator, one ciphertext per ballot field. An empty field is one whose ciphertext is the identity."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Trust and accepted risks"
msgstr "Trust and accepted risks"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The sequencer that holds the key can decrypt every ballot and is the only party able to publish the results."
msgstr "The sequencer that holds the key can decrypt every ballot and is the only party able to publish the results."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Committee keys"
msgstr "Committee keys"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Enough members of one committee round (a threshold of the epoch’s committee) could together decrypt every ballot of the elections keyed on that round, with the organizer secret as well in locked mode. The design trusts the threshold not to collude."
msgstr "Enough members of one committee round (a threshold of the epoch’s committee) could together decrypt every ballot of the elections keyed on that round, with the organizer secret as well in locked mode. The design trusts the threshold not to collude."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "An election’s key belongs to one round’s committee and cannot move to another (there is no resharing). If more than <0/> of its members leave before the election ends, its results are lost."
msgstr "An election’s key belongs to one round’s committee and cannot move to another (there is no resharing). If more than <0/> of its members leave before the election ends, its results are lost."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The committee’s search for a decrypted value stops at <0/> per field. DAVINCI caps results well below that."
msgstr "The committee’s search for a decrypted value stops at <0/> per field. DAVINCI caps results well below that."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Anyone can register applications on the committee, and each takes one of the round’s pool keys, so sixteen cheap calls use a round up. The operators then create the next round at once, and creating elections with a committee key pauses for one round’s setup."
msgstr "Anyone can register applications on the committee, and each takes one of the round’s pool keys, so sixteen cheap calls use a round up. The operators then create the next round at once, and creating elections with a committee key pauses for one round’s setup."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "Between the end and the first decryption request, the organizer can still cancel a Ready or Paused election without having seen the results, the same power it has with a sequencer key. The request itself moves the election to Ended, which only the registry can leave, because the decrypted values become public on the key committee’s contracts before they reach the registry."
msgstr "Between the end and the first decryption request, the organizer can still cancel a Ready or Paused election without having seen the results, the same power it has with a sequencer key. The request itself moves the election to Ended, which only the registry can leave, because the decrypted values become public on the key committee’s contracts before they reach the registry."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "A process page’s <0>Election key</0> tab shows who holds the key and the key itself and, with a committee key, the round (epoch), the application id, the pool key and whether the organizer secret was revealed. The contracts page shows the key committee itself."
msgstr "A process page’s <0>Election key</0> tab shows who holds the key and the key itself and, with a committee key, the round (epoch), the application id, the pool key and whether the organizer secret was revealed. The contracts page shows the key committee itself."

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The key of an election with a committee key"
msgstr "The key of an election with a committee key"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The key of the newest election"
msgstr "The key of the newest election"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
msgid "The key committee behind this registry"
msgstr "The key committee behind this registry"

#: src/pages/learn/content/KeyModes.tsx
#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "Next: <0>how results are produced</0>."
msgstr "Next: <0>how results are produced</0>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Every batch adds its ballots to one encrypted total. When voting ends only that total is decrypted, and the decryption is proven: with a sequencer key by a second proof the registry checks, with a committee key by the key committee’s proofs of each step. The registry records the results only when those proofs hold."
msgstr "Every batch adds its ballots to one encrypted total. When voting ends only that total is decrypted, and the decryption is proven: with a sequencer key by a second proof the registry checks, with a committee key by the key committee’s proofs of each step. The registry records the results only when those proofs hold."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "What gets decrypted"
msgstr "What gets decrypted"

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Each batch adds its ballots to one <0>encrypted total</0>, with one encrypted number per ballot field. Result <1/> is the sum of field <2/> over every counted ballot. The protocol decrypts only the final total, never a single ballot. The key holder could decrypt any earlier total or any ballot in the published data."
msgstr "Each batch adds its ballots to one <0>encrypted total</0>, with one encrypted number per ballot field. Result <1/> is the sum of field <2/> over every counted ballot. The protocol decrypts only the final total, never a single ballot. The key holder could decrypt any earlier total or any ballot in the published data."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "An election can get its results once it is Ended, or once its end time has passed while it is Ready or Paused. How the total is decrypted and proven depends on <0>who holds the key</0>."
msgstr "An election can get its results once it is Ended, or once its end time has passed while it is Ready or Paused. How the total is decrypted and proven depends on <0>who holds the key</0>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "The accumulator is state leaf <0>0x04</0>: 16 ElGamal ciphertexts, one per ballot field."
msgstr "The accumulator is state leaf <0>0x04</0>: 16 ElGamal ciphertexts, one per ballot field."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Sequencer key: a results proof"
msgstr "Sequencer key: a results proof"

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Once the election has ended and its state is final, the sequencer holding the key decrypts the total. It then proves the decryption with a second program, the results program, which checks:"
msgstr "Once the election has ended and its state is final, the sequencer holding the key decrypts the total. It then proves the decryption with a second program, the results program, which checks:"

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "that the key and the encrypted total it used are the ones in the election’s final state;"
msgstr "that the key and the encrypted total it used are the ones in the election’s final state;"

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "that each decrypted number is the correct decryption of its encrypted number;"
msgstr "that each decrypted number is the correct decryption of its encrypted number;"

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "that every value is written in its only valid form, so none has a second encoding."
msgstr "that every value is written in its only valid form, so none has a second encoding."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "The registry records the results only for an election with a sequencer key that has ended, when the proof says every check passed, was made on the election’s latest state and comes from the released results program. It stores one result per ballot field and moves the election to Results."
msgstr "The registry records the results only for an election with a sequencer key that has ended, when the proof says every check passed, was made on the election’s latest state and comes from the released results program. It stores one result per ballot field and moves the election to Results."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Decryption is a bounded search. At creation, and whenever the organizer changes the voter limit (<0>setProcessMaxVoters</0>), the registry requires the largest possible total, the maximum number of voters times the ballot’s maximum value, to stay within the bound below."
msgstr "Decryption is a bounded search. At creation, and whenever the organizer changes the voter limit (<0>setProcessMaxVoters</0>), the registry requires the largest possible total, the maximum number of voters times the ballot’s maximum value, to stay within the bound below."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "The results guest checks that the encryption key (leaf <0>0x03</0>) and the accumulator (leaf <1>0x04</1>) are leaves of the final state tree, one <2>Chaum–Pedersen proof</2> per ciphertext showing each plaintext is the correct decryption under that key, and that every coordinate and scalar is in range."
msgstr "The results guest checks that the encryption key (leaf <0>0x03</0>) and the accumulator (leaf <1>0x04</1>) are leaves of the final state tree, one <2>Chaum–Pedersen proof</2> per ciphertext showing each plaintext is the correct decryption under that key, and that every coordinate and scalar is in range."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "<0>setProcessResults</0> then requires a sequencer-key process that has ended, <1/>, a state root equal to the process’s <2>latestStateRoot</2>, and a PLONK proof verified against <3>resultsProgramVK</3>."
msgstr "<0>setProcessResults</0> then requires a sequencer-key process that has ended, <1/>, a state root equal to the process’s <2>latestStateRoot</2>, and a PLONK proof verified against <3>resultsProgramVK</3>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Committee key: decryption in shares"
msgstr "Committee key: decryption in shares"

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "With a committee key there is no second program. The registry and the key committee do the checking:"
msgstr "With a committee key there is no second program. The registry and the key committee do the checking:"

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "After the end, anyone can ask for the decryption; sequencers ask on their own shortly after the end. The registry checks that the encrypted total is the one in the election’s final state, and moves the election to Ended, which the organizer can no longer change."
msgstr "After the end, anyone can ask for the decryption; sequencers ask on their own shortly after the end. The registry checks that the encrypted total is the one in the election’s final state, and moves the election to Ended, which the organizer can no longer change."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "It skips fields that never received anything (they count as 0, and only an election that never counted a ballot has them) and sends the rest to the committee."
msgstr "It skips fields that never received anything (they count as 0, and only an election that never counted a ballot has them) and sends the rest to the committee."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Committee members post their parts of the decryption, each with a proof. Once enough have, one of them combines the parts, again with a proof, and the decrypted value is stored with the committee. In locked mode none of this starts before the organizer reveals its secret."
msgstr "Committee members post their parts of the decryption, each with a proof. Once enough have, one of them combines the parts, again with a proof, and the decrypted value is stored with the committee. In locked mode none of this starts before the organizer reveals its secret."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Anyone then asks the registry to collect the decrypted values. It stores them in field order and moves the election to Results; until every value is ready, the call is refused."
msgstr "Anyone then asks the registry to collect the decrypted values. It stores them in field order and moves the election to Results; until every value is ready, the call is refused."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "There is no results proof in the committee modes: the committee’s proofs of every step and the registry’s own check of the encrypted total replace it. So the election’s results depend on the committee staying available: once the encrypted total is handed over there is no fallback."
msgstr "There is no results proof in the committee modes: the committee’s proofs of every step and the registry’s own check of the encrypted total replace it. So the election’s results depend on the committee staying available: once the encrypted total is handed over there is no fallback."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "<0>requestResultsDecryption</0> takes the accumulator and its inclusion proof; sequencers call it on their first heartbeat after the end. The registry checks every coordinate is below the field and that the accumulator is leaf <1>0x04</1> under <2>latestStateRoot</2>."
msgstr "<0>requestResultsDecryption</0> takes the accumulator and its inclusion proof; sequencers call it on their first heartbeat after the end. The registry checks every coordinate is below the field and that the accumulator is leaf <1>0x04</1> under <2>latestStateRoot</2>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Skipped fields are the identity in both halves. The rest go to the committee through the adapter, and the registry emits <0>ResultsDecryptionRequested</0>."
msgstr "Skipped fields are the identity in both halves. The rest go to the committee through the adapter, and the registry emits <0>ResultsDecryptionRequested</0>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Each partial decryption carries a Groth16 proof against the member’s committed share, and the combine carries another. The plaintext is stored on the DKG."
msgstr "Each partial decryption carries a Groth16 proof against the member’s committed share, and the combine carries another. The plaintext is stored on the DKG."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "<0>finalizeResultsFromDKG</0> reads the plaintexts. Until every ciphertext is combined it reverts with <1>ResultsNotReady</1>."
msgstr "<0>finalizeResultsFromDKG</0> reads the plaintexts. Until every ciphertext is combined it reverts with <1>ResultsNotReady</1>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "There is no results PLONK in the DKG modes. DKG liveness is election liveness."
msgstr "There is no results PLONK in the DKG modes. DKG liveness is election liveness."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "The results of a finished election and how they were produced"
msgstr "The results of a finished election and how they were produced"

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Processes with results"
msgstr "Processes with results"

#: src/pages/learn/content/Results.tsx
msgid "Next: check it yourself, as a <0>voter</0>, an <1>organizer</1> or an <2>auditor</2>."
msgstr "Next: check it yourself, as a <0>voter</0>, an <1>organizer</1> or an <2>auditor</2>."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "The registry records a batch only if the election is open, the proof is valid and says every check passed, the batch starts from the latest state, its voters were checked against the right list of voters, the voter limit holds and the published data matches the proof. If any check fails the transaction is refused and nothing changes."
msgstr "The registry records a batch only if the election is open, the proof is valid and says every check passed, the batch starts from the latest state, its voters were checked against the right list of voters, the voter limit holds and the published data matches the proof. If any check fails the transaction is refused and nothing changes."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "The call"
msgstr "The call"

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "A sequencer sends a batch to the registry in one transaction, which also carries the batch’s data blobs. Anyone may send it; the checks below decide whether it is recorded (in technical terms, whether the batch settles)."
msgstr "A sequencer sends a batch to the registry in one transaction, which also carries the batch’s data blobs. Anyone may send it; the checks below decide whether it is recorded (in technical terms, whether the batch settles)."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "It is sent as a blob transaction that carries exactly the transition’s blobs, in order."
msgstr "It is sent as a blob transaction that carries exactly the transition’s blobs, in order."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "The checks, in order"
msgstr "The checks, in order"

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "The election exists, is open and is inside its voting window."
msgstr "The election exists, is open and is inside its voting window."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "The proof’s public values have the right size and say every check passed."
msgstr "The proof’s public values have the right size and say every check passed."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "The batch starts from the election’s latest state. A batch built on an older state, such as the loser of a race between two sequencers, is refused here."
msgstr "The batch starts from the election’s latest state. A batch built on an older state, such as the loser of a race between two sequencers, is refused here."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "The voters were checked against a list of voters the election accepts."
msgstr "The voters were checked against a list of voters the election accepts."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "The number of voters before the batch matches the registry’s own count. The proof cannot see the whole state, so the registry supplies it."
msgstr "The number of voters before the batch matches the registry’s own count. The proof cannot see the whole state, so the registry supplies it."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "The batch does not take the election past its maximum number of voters."
msgstr "The batch does not take the election past its maximum number of voters."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "The published data matches the proof: the right number of data blobs, and a fingerprint of them equal to the one in the proof."
msgstr "The published data matches the proof: the right number of data blobs, and a fingerprint of them equal to the one in the proof."

#: src/pages/learn/content/Settlement.tsx
msgid "The proof itself is valid, and was made by the released batch program under the released proving setup."
