msgid "When a slot is written for the first time, because refreshes only touch slots already in use. With a list of voters (origins 1 to 3) the slot follows from the voter’s address, so who voted and when is public."
msgstr "When a slot is written for the first time, because refreshes only touch slots already in use. With a list of voters (origins 1 to 3) the slot follows from the voter’s address, so who voted and when is public."

#: src/pages/learn/content/SilentRevoting.tsx
msgid "How many votes and how many changed votes each batch carried: they are in the proof’s public values and in the registry’s counters."
msgstr "How many votes and how many changed votes each batch carried: they are in the proof’s public values and in the registry’s counters."

#: src/pages/learn/content/SilentRevoting.tsx
msgid "<0>occupied_before</0>, the number of slots written before the batch. The proof cannot see the whole state, so the registry checks it against its own count of voters."
msgstr "<0>occupied_before</0>, the number of slots written before the batch. The proof cannot see the whole state, so the registry checks it against its own count of voters."

#: src/pages/learn/content/SilentRevoting.tsx
msgid "Your own <0>vote id</0>, in the published data of the batch that included it. Vote ids are only ever added, so an earlier vote id stays after you vote again; only the latest ballot of the slot is counted."
msgstr "Your own <0>vote id</0>, in the published data of the batch that included it. Vote ids are only ever added, so an earlier vote id stays after you vote again; only the latest ballot of the slot is counted."

#: src/pages/learn/content/SilentRevoting.tsx
msgid "What stays hidden"
msgstr "What stays hidden"

#: src/pages/learn/content/SilentRevoting.tsx
msgid "Which slots already in use were changed and which were only refreshed: in the published data they look the same."
msgstr "Which slots already in use were changed and which were only refreshed: in the published data they look the same."

#: src/pages/learn/content/SilentRevoting.tsx
msgid "Which slots got a changed vote, even though the number of changed votes is public."
msgstr "Which slots got a changed vote, even though the number of changed votes is public."

#: src/pages/learn/content/SilentRevoting.tsx
msgid "Which stored ballot matches the one a voter sent, without the batch’s secret."
msgstr "Which stored ballot matches the one a voter sent, without the batch’s secret."

#: src/pages/learn/content/SilentRevoting.tsx
msgid "One known limit: re-encryption scalars are SHA-256 digests reduced modulo the BN254 prime, which leaves them <0/> away from uniform modulo the subgroup order."
msgstr "One known limit: re-encryption scalars are SHA-256 digests reduced modulo the BN254 prime, which leaves them <0/> away from uniform modulo the subgroup order."

