msgid "The proof itself is valid"
msgstr "The proof itself is valid"

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Each data blob holds the data the proof describes"
msgstr "Each data blob holds the data the proof describes"

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Inside the proof, every vote was checked: its proof, its signature, the voter’s place on the list and how it was stored. A batch with a single failed check is refused."
msgstr "Inside the proof, every vote was checked: its proof, its signature, the voter’s place on the list and how it was stored. A batch with a single failed check is refused."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The public values (`publicValues`) must be exactly 512 bytes and report that every check passed, or the call reverts with `CircuitFailed`. A batch the proven program rejected can still be proven, but it can never be recorded."
msgstr "The public values (`publicValues`) must be exactly 512 bytes and report that every check passed, or the call reverts with `CircuitFailed`. A batch the proven program rejected can still be proven, but it can never be recorded."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Decode the call’s data. The second value is `publicValues`, one 8-byte little-endian word per register, so it opens with the words below: `ok` is 1, then an empty fail mask."
msgstr "Decode the call’s data. The second value is `publicValues`, one 8-byte little-endian word per register, so it opens with the words below: `ok` is 1, then an empty fail mask."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Each batch builds on the one before, so no batch can be skipped, replayed or forked."
msgstr "Each batch builds on the one before, so no batch can be skipped, replayed or forked."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The state before the batch (registers 2 to 9) must be the process’s `latestStateRoot`, or the call reverts with `InvalidStateRoot`. The first batch starts at the starting state (the genesis root) the registry computed when the process was created."
msgstr "The state before the batch (registers 2 to 9) must be the process’s `latestStateRoot`, or the call reverts with `InvalidStateRoot`. The first batch starts at the starting state (the genesis root) the registry computed when the process was created."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Read the registry one block before the batch was recorded: `latestStateRoot`, the fourth value, is where this batch had to start. Reading a past block needs an RPC node that keeps old state."
msgstr "Read the registry one block before the batch was recorded: `latestStateRoot`, the fourth value, is where this batch had to start. Reading a past block needs an RPC node that keeps old state."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Every voter in the batch was on this election’s list of voters. Here a contract keeps the list, so the registry asks it."
msgstr "Every voter in the batch was on this election’s list of voters. Here a contract keeps the list, so the registry asks it."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The registry asks the census contract for `getRootBlockNumber(root)`, with the list fingerprint from registers 20 to 27, bytes reversed. The contract answers the last block that fingerprint was valid: the current block for its current list, the block it was replaced in for an older one, 0 for one it never held. The answer must be non-zero, no later than the block of the batch and no earlier than the block the process was created in, or the call reverts with `InvalidCensusRoot`."
msgstr "The registry asks the census contract for `getRootBlockNumber(root)`, with the list fingerprint from registers 20 to 27, bytes reversed. The contract answers the last block that fingerprint was valid: the current block for its current list, the block it was replaced in for an older one, 0 for one it never held. The answer must be non-zero, no later than the block of the batch and no earlier than the block the process was created in, or the call reverts with `InvalidCensusRoot`."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Ask the census contract yourself, at the block the batch was recorded in. The explorer cannot recompute this one from the registry’s events."
msgstr "Ask the census contract yourself, at the block the batch was recorded in. The explorer cannot recompute this one from the registry’s events."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Every voter in the batch was on this election’s list of voters, and on no other list."
msgstr "Every voter in the batch was on this election’s list of voters, and on no other list."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Registers 20 to 27, with their bytes reversed, must equal the census root stored for the process, or the call reverts with `InvalidCensusRoot`. For a credential service (CSP) the root is the service’s signing address. An updatable list accepts only its current root, so a batch proven against a replaced list stops being accepted."
msgstr "Registers 20 to 27, with their bytes reversed, must equal the census root stored for the process, or the call reverts with `InvalidCensusRoot`. For a credential service (CSP) the root is the service’s signing address. An updatable list accepts only its current root, so a batch proven against a replaced list stops being accepted."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "In the same registry read, the census is the sixteenth value; its second field is the root this batch had to be proven against."
msgstr "In the same registry read, the census is the sixteenth value; its second field is the root this batch had to be proven against."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The proof and the registry agree on how many people had voted before this batch. That number sets how many ballots the batch must re-encrypt to hide who changed their vote."
msgstr "The proof and the registry agree on how many people had voted before this batch. That number sets how many ballots the batch must re-encrypt to hide who changed their vote."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Register 42 must equal `votersCount`, the ballot slots written before this batch, or the call reverts with `InvalidOccupiedBefore`. The proven program cannot see the whole state, so it takes this number as input to size the silent refreshes; the registry pins it to its own count."
msgstr "Register 42 must equal `votersCount`, the ballot slots written before this batch, or the call reverts with `InvalidOccupiedBefore`. The proven program cannot see the whole state, so it takes this number as input to size the silent refreshes; the registry pins it to its own count."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "`votersCount` is the ninth value of the registry read one block before the batch was recorded."
msgstr "`votersCount` is the ninth value of the registry read one block before the batch was recorded."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The registry’s counts of voters and changed votes move exactly as the proof says."
msgstr "The registry’s counts of voters and changed votes move exactly as the proof says."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The registry adds the new voters (votes minus changed votes, registers 18 and 19) to `votersCount` and refuses a batch that would pass `maxVoters` (`MaxVotersReached`). It adds the changed votes to `overwrittenVotesCount` and emits the new totals in `ProcessStateTransitioned`."
msgstr "The registry adds the new voters (votes minus changed votes, registers 18 and 19) to `votersCount` and refuses a batch that would pass `maxVoters` (`MaxVotersReached`). It adds the changed votes to `overwrittenVotesCount` and emits the new totals in `ProcessStateTransitioned`."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "List the process’s batch events. Each log’s data is `oldStateRoot`, `newStateRoot`, `newVotersCount`, `newOverwrittenVotesCount` and `nBlobs`, 32 bytes each: from one log to the next, `newVotersCount` grows by the batch’s new voters, and the same list shows each batch starting where the last one ended."
msgstr "List the process’s batch events. Each log’s data is `oldStateRoot`, `newStateRoot`, `newVotersCount`, `newOverwrittenVotesCount` and `nBlobs`, 32 bytes each: from one log to the next, `newVotersCount` grows by the batch’s new voters, and the same list shows each batch starting where the last one ended."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Everything the batch needs to publish is attached to the transaction, with nothing missing and nothing extra."
msgstr "Everything the batch needs to publish is attached to the transaction, with nothing missing and nothing extra."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "`NBlobs` (register 36) must be non-zero; the commitment, evaluation and proof arrays must each hold that many entries, and the transaction may carry no blob past them (`NoBlobs`, `BlobCountMismatch`)."
msgstr "`NBlobs` (register 36) must be non-zero; the commitment, evaluation and proof arrays must each hold that many entries, and the transaction may carry no blob past them (`NoBlobs`, `BlobCountMismatch`)."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The transaction’s `blobVersionedHashes` lists one hash per blob."
msgstr "The transaction’s `blobVersionedHashes` lists one hash per blob."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The data the transaction publishes is the data that was proven, not something swapped in afterwards."
msgstr "The data the transaction publishes is the data that was proven, not something swapped in afterwards."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "One fingerprint over the commitments and evaluations in the call must equal the blobs digest in registers 28 to 35, or the call reverts with `InvalidBlobsDigest`. That ties what the transaction carries to what the proven program computed from the data it checked."
msgstr "One fingerprint over the commitments and evaluations in the call must equal the blobs digest in registers 28 to 35, or the call reverts with `InvalidBlobsDigest`. That ties what the transaction carries to what the proven program computed from the data it checked."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Hash the commitments and evaluations in order: the result is the blobs digest in the public values."
msgstr "Hash the commitments and evaluations in order: the result is the blobs digest in the public values."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The proof was made by the published program, for exactly these values. A proof of any other program, or with any value changed, is refused."
msgstr "The proof was made by the published program, for exactly these values. A proof of any other program, or with any value changed, is refused."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The verifier contract (`ZiskVerifier`, its `verifySnarkProof`) must accept the proof under the two keys fixed in the registry, `batchProgramVK` and `rootCVadcopFinal`, or the call reverts with `InvalidProof`. The verifier hashes both keys with the public values into the one input the proof must match."
msgstr "The verifier contract (`ZiskVerifier`, its `verifySnarkProof`) must accept the proof under the two keys fixed in the registry, `batchProgramVK` and `rootCVadcopFinal`, or the call reverts with `InvalidProof`. The verifier hashes both keys with the public values into the one input the proof must match."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Make the same call: it returns `0x` when the proof verifies and reverts otherwise."
msgstr "Make the same call: it returns `0x` when the proof verifies and reverts otherwise."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The fingerprints of the published data the proof used are those of the data blobs this transaction really carries."
msgstr "The fingerprints of the published data the proof used are those of the data blobs this transaction really carries."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "A blob’s versioned hash, what `BLOBHASH` returns, is built from its commitment as below. The point-evaluation precompile rejects a commitment that does not match the transaction’s hash."
msgstr "A blob’s versioned hash, what `BLOBHASH` returns, is built from its commitment as below. The point-evaluation precompile rejects a commitment that does not match the transaction’s hash."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Hash each commitment and replace the first byte with 01: that is the transaction’s versioned hash."
msgstr "Hash each commitment and replace the first byte with 01: that is the transaction’s versioned hash."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Each data blob on the chain holds the data the proof was made for, checked at a point nobody could choose in advance."
msgstr "Each data blob on the chain holds the data the proof was made for, checked at a point nobody could choose in advance."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "For every blob the registry calls the point-evaluation precompile with the versioned hash, the point `z` below, the evaluation `y` and the KZG proof, or the call reverts with `InvalidBlobOpening`. The point hashes the process id padded to 32 bytes, the fingerprint of the state before with its bytes reversed, and the 48-byte commitment. The proven program evaluated the blob it laid out itself at the same point, so the blobs on the chain are the ones the proof covers."
msgstr "For every blob the registry calls the point-evaluation precompile with the versioned hash, the point `z` below, the evaluation `y` and the KZG proof, or the call reverts with `InvalidBlobOpening`. The point hashes the process id padded to 32 bytes, the fingerprint of the state before with its bytes reversed, and the 48-byte commitment. The proven program evaluated the blob it laid out itself at the same point, so the blobs on the chain are the ones the proof covers."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Send the same 192 bytes to the precompile: it answers 4096 and the BLS12-381 modulus when the opening holds, and fails otherwise."
msgstr "Send the same 192 bytes to the precompile: it answers 4096 and the BLS12-381 modulus when the opening holds, and fails otherwise."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The election’s new state is the one the proof arrived at; the next batch has to start from it."
msgstr "The election’s new state is the one the proof arrived at; the next batch has to start from it."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "Once every check above passed, the registry stores registers 10 to 17 as the new `latestStateRoot` and emits it as `newStateRoot`."
msgstr "Once every check above passed, the registry stores registers 10 to 17 as the new `latestStateRoot` and emits it as `newStateRoot`."

#: src/pages/transition/checks.ts
msgid "The `ProcessStateTransitioned` log in the transaction receipt carries `newStateRoot` as the second 32-byte word of its data."
msgstr "The `ProcessStateTransitioned` log in the transaction receipt carries `newStateRoot` as the second 32-byte word of its data."

