msgstr "<0>setProcessCensus</0>: only for an updatable Merkle census (origin 2), before the end. Batches proven against the old list are no longer accepted."

#: src/pages/verify/election/index.tsx
msgid "<0>setProcessMetadata</0>: a new document address and its SHA-256, while Ready or Paused and before the end; then the description is frozen. Every version stays on the log, and a change made while voting was open is flagged to everyone who checks the election."
msgstr "<0>setProcessMetadata</0>: a new document address and its SHA-256, while Ready or Paused and before the end; then the description is frozen. Every version stays on the log, and a change made while voting was open is flagged to everyone who checks the election."

#: src/pages/verify/election/index.tsx
msgid "No batch is recorded after the end time. With a sequencer key, the node that holds the key publishes the results once the election has ended; it is the only one that can. With a key committee (a DKG key) anyone can ask the committee to decrypt, and sequencers do on their first heartbeat after the end; in locked mode the decryption waits for your reveal (<0>revealProcessKey</0> on the registry). The results tab shows how the results were produced."
msgstr "No batch is recorded after the end time. With a sequencer key, the node that holds the key publishes the results once the election has ended; it is the only one that can. With a key committee (a DKG key) anyone can ask the committee to decrypt, and sequencers do on their first heartbeat after the end; in locked mode the decryption waits for your reveal (<0>revealProcessKey</0> on the registry). The results tab shows how the results were produced."

#: src/pages/verify/election/index.tsx
msgid "Keep the organizer secret of a locked election. Without it the committee never decrypts the results."
msgstr "Keep the organizer secret of a locked election. Without it the committee never decrypts the results."

